# Code owners for spectrafit-core.
#
# TWO COPIES EXIST ON PURPOSE: this file and /CODEOWNERS (repo root). GitLab
# (the primary remote / merge target, see CONTRIBUTING.md) never reads
# .github/ — only the repo root, docs/, or .gitlab/ — so a CODEOWNERS living
# only here would be inert on the source of truth and would only ever govern
# PRs on the disposable GitHub mirror. Keep both files' content in sync by
# hand; there is no generator for this today.
#
# GitHub matches this file only as `CODEOWNERS` (or `.github/CODEOWNERS`), and on
# a case-insensitive filesystem a lowercase `codeowners` is the SAME file locally
# while being invisible to GitHub. Keep the name uppercase.
#
# Single maintainer today; every other committer is a CI automation account. The
# per-area lines are not redundant with the catch-all — they are where a second
# maintainer gets added without having to reason about the whole tree.

*                       @Anselmoo

# Rust solver workspace
/crates/                @Anselmoo

# Python engine, oracles and the benchmark harness
/python/                @Anselmoo

# Web dashboard
/web/                   @Anselmoo

# Release, CI and publication tooling
/scripts/               @Anselmoo
/.github/               @Anselmoo
/.gitlab/               @Anselmoo

# Manuscript and its reproducible artifacts
/manuscript/            @Anselmoo
